From: Aegir <dev@aegir.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] libcxx: initialize __chash for GCC's flow analysis

GCC's -Wmaybe-uninitialized cannot see that __chash is assigned in the block
below the call to __rehash_unique, so at -O1 and above it refuses the file
under -Werror and the hosted userland cannot be optimized. Initializing it
silences a false positive by making the code explicit; upstream does the same.

diff --git a/libcxx/include/__hash_table b/libcxx/include/__hash_table
--- a/libcxx/include/__hash_table
+++ b/libcxx/include/__hash_table
@@ -1478,7 +1478,7 @@
   size_type __bc  = bucket_count();
   bool __inserted = false;
   __next_pointer __nd;
-  size_t __chash;
+  size_t __chash = 0;
   if (__bc != 0) {
     __chash = std::__constrain_hash(__hash, __bc);
     __nd    = __bucket_list_[__chash];
